# An undo outlives a look at another workspace: delete a note, move to the workspace list, down
# to the other workspace (which opens it) and back up, then u still puts the note back.
# tests/drive.rs adds the second workspace to the list and checks the file and the trash.
env COLD_LAVA_EDITOR=none
wait-for example-workspace 35 notes
keys p lava
wait-for Lava
keys enter
wait-for Concepts/Lava  reading
keys d
wait-for Delete Concepts/Lava?
keys y
wait-for deleted Lava · u undo
wait-for example-workspace 34 notes
keys esc
wait-gone reading · Esc / q back
keys h h h
keys j
wait-for elsewhere 1 note
keys k
wait-for example-workspace 34 notes
keys l
keys u
wait-for restored Concepts/Lava.md
wait-for example-workspace 35 notes
wait-for Molten rock that reaches the surface.
keys esc
wait-for ? help  q quit
keys q
exits 0
